.TH "SCCFM-CLI POLICIES ACCESS-RULE CREATE" "1" "2026-08-24" "0.39.4" "sccfm-cli policies access-rule create Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-policies\-access-rule\-create \- Create an ASA access rule.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli policies access-rule create
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create an ASA access rule.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-access\-group\-uid\fP TEXT
UID of the access group.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-entity\-uid\fP TEXT
UID of the device or manager.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-index\fP INTEGER
Position of the rule in the ordered list.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-rule\-action\fP [permit|deny]
Rule action.  [default: PERMIT]
.TP
\fB\-\-remark\fP TEXT
Human-readable description of the rule.
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-network\fP TEXT
Source network object name.
.TP
\fB\-\-destination\-network\fP TEXT
Destination network object name.
.TP
\fB\-\-protocol\fP TEXT
Protocol (e.g. tcp, udp, ip).
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-port\fP TEXT
Source port or port range.
.TP
\fB\-\-destination\-port\fP TEXT
Destination port or port range.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fP TEXT
Log level.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-interval\fP INTEGER
Log interval in seconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-active\fP / \-\-inactive
Whether the rule is active.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Run a preflight check without performing the operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
